t\nOnline Graduate Certificates\nHow to Apply\nTuition & Fees\nFaculty\nStudent Life\nContact Us\nExecutive\nFaculty & Research\nFaculty Directory\nResearch\nSpeaker Series\nJournals & Books\nCareer Services\nFor Students\nFor Alumni\nFor Employers\nEvents\nOur Team\nStudent Life\nLife at O\u2019Neill\nLife in Bloomington\nPrecollege Programs\nFor International Students\nResilience and Wellbeing Initiative\nO\u2019Neill International\nLeadership Opportunities\nStudent Organizations\nVirtual Tour\nAbout\nDean\u2019s Welcome\nLeadership\nStrategic Goals and Progress\nAbout Paul H. O'Neill\nPaul H. O\u2019Neill Center for Leadership in Public Service\nEnvironment, Climate, and Sustainability\nMission, Vision, and Values\nRankings\nSchool Profile\nGlobal and International Partnerships\nBelonging, Engagement, and Success\nBloomington & Indianapolis\nCareers at O'Neill\nAdministration & Staff Directory\nDean\u2019s Council\nExecutives in Residence\nHistory\nAlumni & Giving\nContact\nEvents\nNews\nIU Indy\nCurrent Students\nHome\nDoctoral\nStudent Funding\nEnvironmental Science Funding\nEnvironmental Science Funding\nFunding assistance for your environmental science degree\nStudents admitted to the O\u2019Neill School Environmental Science Ph.D. program usually receive a 100% tuition and fee waiver, university-paid health insurance, and a stipend as part of a student academic appointment. The stipend is updated annually according to a university established cost of living adjustment schedule ($30,000 for AY2026-2027, including summer months).\nA student academic appointment (SAA) consists of a 20-hour per week work assignment as a Research Assistant (RA) in your major advisor\u2019s laboratory, for all 12 months of the year. Being assigned as an Associate Instructor (AI), the instructor of record, for an undergraduate course is possible, but less common.\nThe academic appointment is typically awarded for the duration of the program provided the assigned appointee duties are being fulfilled, a GPA of 3.0 is maintained, and satisfactory progress is made toward the degree.\nThe O\u2019Neill School Environmental Science Ph.D. degree is awarded by the Indiana University Graduate School Bloomington. For additional information, see University Graduate School Bloomington.\nRoy W. Shin Fellowship\nContact us\nWhy O'Neill?\nDegrees\nHow to Apply\nStudent Funding\nEnvironmental Science Funding\nPublic Affairs Funding\nBrass Fellowship in Public Affairs\nRoy W. Shin Fellowship\nOn the Job Market\nRecent Placements\nCurrent Students\nDissertations\nContact\nPaul H. O\u2019Neill School of Public and Environmental Affairs social media channels\nGive to the O\u2019Neill School\nTwitter\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYouTube\nLinkedIn\nAdditional links and resources\nREPORT A BIAS INCIDENT | O\u2019NEILL SCHOOL DOCUMENTS | FACULTY RESEARCH RESOURCES | INTRANET\nAccessibility |\nCollege Scorecard |\nOpen to All |\nPrivacy Notice\n|\nCopyright \u00a9 2026\nThe Trustees of\nIndiana University", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/doctoral/cost-financial-aid/environmental-science-funding.html#content"], ["Skip to Main Navigation", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/doctoral/cost-financial-aid/environmental-science-funding.html#nav-main"], ["Skip to Search", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/doctoral/cost-financial-aid/environmental-science-funding.html#search"], ["Indiana University Bloomington Indiana University Bloomington IU Bloomington", "https://bloomington.iu.edu"], ["", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/search"], ["Undergraduate", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/undergraduate/index.html"], ["Why O'Neill", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/undergraduate/why-oneill/index.html"], ["High-impact Practices", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/undergraduate/why-oneill/hip.html"], ["Accelerated Degrees", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/undergraduate/academic-enrichment/accelerated-masters/index.html"], ["Degrees & Majors", "https://oneill.indiana.edu/undergraduate/degrees-majors/in